fields: {'summary': 'The logs demos are not working', 'issuetype': {'self': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issuetype/1', 'id': '1', 'description': 'A problem which impairs or prevents the functions of the product.', 'iconUrl': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/viewavatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=21133&avatarType=issuetype', 'name': 'Bug', 'subtask': False, 'avatarId': 21133}, 'description': 'See https://lists.apache.org/thread/ppvrrspmc473ox872v51fcj6s9yvmsxl', 'comment': {'comments': [{'self': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/13647740/comment/18072661', 'id': '18072661', 'author': {'self': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=danwatford', 'name': 'danwatford', 'key': 'danwatford', 'avatarUrls': {'48x48': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=danwatford&avatarId=41038', '24x24': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=danwatford&avatarId=41038', '16x16': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=danwatford&avatarId=41038', '32x32': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=danwatford&avatarId=41038'}, 'displayName': 'Daniel Watford', 'active': True, 'timeZone': 'Europe/London'}, 'body': "When we build our docker images, we add a new user, named ofbiz, to the image.

Using this command we can see that the uid (User ID) and gid (Group ID) for this user is 1000:

{{root@ofbiz-ec2-or:/home/ofbizdocker/demo-next# docker compose exec ofbiz grep ofbiz /etc/passwd}}
{{ofbiz:x:1000:1000::/home/ofbiz:/bin/sh}}

However, when our demos are running, we see that a different UID is used for the ofbiz processes:

{{root@ofbiz-ec2-or:/home/ofbizdocker/demo-next# ps aux | grep bin/java | cut --bytes=-80}}
{{101000 \xa0 1179752 18.1 \xa04.5 6990356 1496732 ? \xa0 \xa0 Ssl \xa015:08 \xa0 4:21 /opt/java/ope}}
{{101000 \xa0 1180722 \xa07.8 \xa02.2 6977472 735680 ? \xa0 \xa0 \xa0Ssl \xa015:11 \xa0 1:37 /opt/java/ope}}
{{101000 \xa0 1181621 \xa08.1 \xa02.5 6974176 830744 ? \xa0 \xa0 \xa0Ssl \xa015:14 \xa0 1:28 /opt/java/ope}}
{{root \xa0 \xa0 1184465 \xa00.0 \xa00.0 \xa0 7088 \xa02164 pts/1 \xa0 \xa0S+ \xa0 15:32 \xa0 0:00 grep --color=}}

{{The first column is the effective uid of the process, a value of 101000.}}

{{Even though the container image has configured the ofbiz user to have uid 1000, docker cannot allow a process to run with that id on the host as, if the process theoretically breaks out of the container, it would have access to all the resources on the host that are available to user with uid 1000.}}

Instead, docker applies subordinate uid and gids to the processes in the container. These are configured in the following files:

{{root@ofbiz-ec2-or:/home/ofbizdocker/demo-next# cat /etc/subuid}}
{{dockremap:100000:65536}}
{{root@ofbiz-ec2-or:/home/ofbizdocker/demo-next# cat /etc/subgid}}
{{dockremap:100000:65536}}

So user ids are mapped to the range 100000-165536, and group ids are mapped to the range 100000-165536.

Taking the container's uid of 1000 and remapping to the above range gives a uid of 101000, matching the `ps aux` above. The same mapping happens for groups.

In order to have log files written, our logs directories for our demo applications needs to be writable by uid 101000. For the moment I have made the log directories writable by all, but there is probably a better solution we should employ longer-term.", 'updateAuthor': {'self': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=danwatford', 'name': 'danwatford', 'key': 'danwatford', 'avatarUrls': {'48x48': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=danwatford&avatarId=41038', '24x24': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=danwatford&avatarId=41038', '16x16': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=danwatford&avatarId=41038', '32x32': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=danwatford&avatarId=41038'}, 'displayName': 'Daniel Watford', 'active': True, 'timeZone': 'Europe/London'}, 'created': '2026-04-10T15:42:26.142+0000', 'updated': '2026-04-10T15:42:26.142+0000'}, {'self': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/13647740/comment/18072669', 'id': '18072669', 'author': {'self': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jleroux', 'name': 'jleroux', 'key': 'jacques.le.roux', 'avatarUrls': {'48x48': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jacques.le.roux&avatarId=29375', '24x24': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jacques.le.roux&avatarId=29375', '16x16': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jacques.le.roux&avatarId=29375', '32x32': 'https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jacques.le.roux&avatarId=29375'}, 'displayName': 'Jacques Le Roux', 'active': True, 'timeZone': 'Europe/Paris'}, 'body': "Thanks Daniel,

